{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T03:33:50.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2nwcgg+pm-dhlij3+pm-x9r2h3","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-f0s4g8"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"PmClient.schemaAddField reads a whitespace-only cliFlag as omitted and registers the default flag, while pm schema add-field --cli-flag ' ' refuses it with schema_field_flag_invalid"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-27 while fixing pm-2nwcgg. After that fix, the CLI refuses a supplied --cli-flag or --alias that normalizes to nothing. Through the SDK, new PmClient({ pmRoot }).schemaAddField('review_owner', { type: 'string', commands: ['list'], cliFlag: ' ' }) resolves and registers the default --review-owner flag, while cliFlag '--' and alias ['  '] are refused as on the CLI. So somewhere on the PmClient.runTyped path a whitespace-only string option is dropped before runSchemaAddField sees it. Find where, and decide whether the transport should keep a supplied blank string for every command (as argv does) or whether schema options need their own exception. Duplicate check: searched blank option string omitted, whitespace option SDK transport; no open item covers it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","schema","transport-parity"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-27T03:33:50.298Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T03:33:50.298Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Reproduce the SDK and CLI divergence and name the transport stage that drops the blank string; PmClient.schemaAddField with a whitespace-only cliFlag is refused with schema_field_flag_invalid as the CLI refuses it, or the transport rule is documented with a reason; A parity spec drives the CLI and the SDK with the same blank spelling"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A blank cliFlag gets the same verdict through the SDK and the CLI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The SDK registers the default flag; the CLI refuses with schema_field_flag_invalid"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-2nwcgg","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-27T03:33:50.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2fbe4c44fcb82c178ed457088cba010ccc0f8c7f639638b8f91b7a9c653d7760","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a7010e2605b24505f22119c94593bb552334fcfac20b13442e478416172b0bc2"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T04:49:35.617Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T04:49:35.617Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-27T04:49:35.617Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Stage located by the Codex review of the field-admission branch (2026-11-27), confirmed by reading the code: the SDK schema dispatch (createMcpSchemaContext in src/sdk/runtime/schema.ts) reads aliases through readRuntimeStringArray (src/sdk/runtime-input.ts), which maps entries with String and drops every empty one, so alias [''] never reaches add-field; cliFlag goes through readRuntimeString, which drops a blank value the same way. A two-space alias survives (it is not empty), which is why it was refused through the SDK while cliFlag ' ' was not. A fix can keep raw entries for add-field's cliFlag and alias, or decide the transport rule for every command."}]}],"before_hash":"2fbe4c44fcb82c178ed457088cba010ccc0f8c7f639638b8f91b7a9c653d7760","after_hash":"61848701d8de248d83c937cead4ce4939bd5dc19d8dd93b3a9a6b8580c730fa6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e0a3b4a18844c51a8b1216e0981f92e223b0b13a518160773e6e7a96ab096be8"}
